  "theologicalNotes": "Three Forms of Unity (Belgic Confession, Heidelberg Catechism, Canons of Dort). Covenant theology. Infant baptism. Amillennial. Pastor Bradd L. Nymeyer. Address: 6159 Riverside Drive, Chino, CA 91710. Website: http://www.chinourc.org.",
  "description": "First United Reformed Church in Chino, California, was established in 1958 and gathers on Riverside Drive as a congregation of the United Reformed Churches in North America. The church confesses Scripture as inspired, inerrant, and the supreme authority over all matters of faith and godliness, and her officers fully subscribe to the Three Forms of Unity: the Belgic Confession, the Heidelberg Catechism, and the Canons of Dort, alongside the three ecumenical Creeds. Lord's Day worship at 9:30 and 6:00 is shaped by Reformed convictions, covenantal baptism of believing households, and the regular celebration of the Lord's Supper. A council of elders and deacons governs the congregation.",
